  "finding": "8 of 8 primitives are rejected by the anti-overfit gates as indistinguishable from shuffled data, and 0 return no verdict at all for want of data \u2014 which is not a pass. 0 clear every gate, of which 0 still lose money after the 12bps round trip. 8 of 8 are net-negative after fees regardless of gate. Statistical structure and tradeable edge are different things, and on this venue the difference is the fee.",
  "failure_cases": {
    "definition": "primitives on which the anti-overfit gates could not return a verdict at all",
