    "of_primitives": 8,
    "factors": [],
    "why": "the deflated-Sharpe gate needs a trial count and a variance across trials; with too few observations the variance is undefined and the gate raises rather than returning NaN. The refusal is the designed behaviour \u2014 vectorbt's own deflated_sharpe_ratio silently returns NaN on a single trial, which a caller filtering with a negated comparison then admits \u2014 but a gate that cannot decide has protected nothing on that input, and saying so is the point.",
    "scope_statement": "NOT CLAIMED: that these two are the only inputs the gates cannot handle \u2014 they are the ones this instrument and window produced. NOT CLAIMED: that a refusal is a defect; it is the correct behaviour and it is also not a pass, which is why it is counted here rather than folded into the rejected count."
